      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An escrow agent is a neutral third-party representative who holds and manages funds on behalf of the buyer and seller until the sale is complete. They ensure that the payment is made to the seller and that any outstanding obligations, such as repairs or credits, are fulfilled. The escrow agent collects and releases funds according to the terms of the contract, reducing the risk of disputes between the parties. This service helps protect both the buyer and seller from potential issues and provides an added layer of security.",
