      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow agents are tied to the transaction and have a vested interest in completing it successfully. In terms of safeguards, they often have to disclose the contract details to the buyer and state associations, and in the US, they typically have to follow state-specific regulations and laws related to escrow accounts. Additionally, escrow agents work under a neutral escrow agreement that requires them to deliver funds by the deadline. This accountability and oversight help prevent any potential misappropriation of funds.",
